  "description": "PostgreSQL support for Reeve.Workloads: the library's own migrations, the persistence conventions — jsonb for the JSON columns and the active-row filters on the partial unique indexes — and an advisory-lock leader election for the workload engine. The migrations and the conventions need no wiring at all; AddEntityFrameworkStores finds them both when the context runs on Npgsql, and a host writes none of its own. The election is one call, AddPostgreSqlLeaderElection(), because a registration runs before any context can report a provider.",
